       "text": "ANGLE ID: LI1-W48-09\nSTATUS: Copy complete\nCORE ARGUMENT: PMAR, Redfin and Realtor.com publish different Monroe County figures because they measure different things. Mixing them in client conversations creates contradictions.\nAUDIENCE: Agents, lenders, appraisers, attorneys\nTAKEAWAY: Cite one source per claim, name the month and say whether it's sold or asking.\nFORMAT: Text post · Effort: Low\nSOURCES:\n• PMAR Monthly Indicators, October 2026 (Monroe County, all residential; ShowingTime, current as of Nov 9, 2026). Same source as last week's published plan.\n• PMAR Monroe County closings, September 2026: −18.3% YoY (as published in last week's LI1, from PMAR Monthly Indicators)\n• Redfin Monroe County: September 2026 sales 216 vs 251 (−13.9%), 'All Home Types'; median sale price about $328,764, window unclear. PARTIAL.\n• Realtor.com Monroe County page: median list price about $379,973 (+4.46% YoY), undated; summary mislabels a monthly change as yearly. PARTIAL: use only as 'a listing site shows'.\nBEFORE POSTING:\n• Not a criticism of any site. Frame as definitions and coverage, not errors (except the one mislabel, which isn't named)."
