       "text": "Three websites, three Monroe County 'median prices' this fall:\n\n• Pocono Mountains Association of REALTORS®: $350,000 median sale price, October\n• Redfin: about $329,000 median sale price, with the period labeled inconsistently\n• A national listing site: about $380,000 median list price, undated\n\nSame county. Different measures, periods and coverage. Even closings differ: Redfin shows September sales down 13.9% year over year; PMAR shows September closings down 18.3%.\n\nNone of them is 'wrong.' The problem starts when we mix them. A seller who hears $380K from a portal and $350K from us thinks someone is misleading them, when one number is asking prices and the other is sales.\n\nMy rule for client conversations: one source per claim, the month it covers, and whether it's sold or asking. For Monroe, I default to PMAR's Monthly Indicators because they come from local MLS data and are consistent month to month.\n\nWhich source do you default to, and why?\n\nAlexa Sanchez, REALTOR® · PA License No. RS326383 · Smart Way America Realty"
