       "label": "Publish-ready copy",
       "kind": "text",
       "text": "If your home is listed over the holidays, here's what to set up this week:\n\n1. Showing access while you're away. Who has the key or lockbox code, and who can say yes to a last-minute showing? A buyer touring the day after Thanksgiving is usually serious.\n2. Heat and lights. Keep the house warm and the lights on timers, even if you're at family's for the weekend. It gets dark before 5.\n3. Decorations, lightly. A wreath and a few lights look welcoming. A living room full of boxes and a tree that blocks the fireplace makes rooms look smaller.\n4. A snow plan. If it snows mid-showing week, the driveway and walk need to be clear without you.\n\nA few small arrangements keep a holiday listing from losing a week.\n\nHappy Thanksgiving.\n\nAlexa Sanchez · PA License No. RS326383 · Smart Way America Realty · 528 Seven Bridges Rd, Suite 108, East Stroudsburg, PA 18301 · (570) 688-8147"
