       "text": "ANGLE ID: YT1-W48-02\nSTATUS: Copy complete · needs filming · rate recheck\nCORE ARGUMENT: Rates, national contracts and statewide sales all slowed this fall; Monroe slowed earlier and harder in closings, while prices held up and October contracts dipped only slightly.\nAUDIENCE: Monroe homeowners deciding about a winter or spring sale\nTAKEAWAY: Use local numbers, price for this year's buyer budget, and watch November's contracts.\nFORMAT: Talking head + graphics, 16:9, ~5 min (~700 words) · Effort: Moderate\nSOURCES:\n• Freddie Mac PMMS, Nov 19, 2026: 30-yr 7.28% (Nov 12: 7.11%; a year ago: 6.26%) — https://www.freddiemac.com/pmms\n• NAR Pending Home Sales, October 2026 (national): −4.7% MoM, −16.7% YoY, via RISMedia, Nov 18, 2026 — https://www.rismedia.com/2026/11/18/pending-sales-down-over-16-percent-as-2026-market-craters/\n• PAR September 2026 housing report (released Oct 21, 2026): about 10,260 PA sales vs 11,345 a year earlier (about −9.5%); median $315,000 (+6% YoY), via MyChesCo — https://www.mychesco.com/a/news/pennsylvania/pennsylvania-home-sales-fall-10-as-prices-retreat/\n• PMAR Monthly Indicators, October 2026 (Monroe County, all residential; ShowingTime, current as of Nov 9, 2026). Same source as last week's published plan.\n• PMAR Monroe County pending sales YoY: Jul −10.6%, Aug −7.9%, Sep −14.6%, Oct −3.8% (201 vs 209) (as published in last week's LI1)\n• PMAR Monroe County closings, September 2026: −18.3% YoY (as published in last week's LI1, from PMAR Monthly Indicators)\n• Payment math: $280,000 loan (80% of the $350K Monroe median, same base as last week's IG5), 30-yr fixed, principal and interest only: $1,883.58 at 7.11% → $1,915.79 at 7.28% (+$32.22/mo). A year ago at 6.26%: $1,725.83 (+$189.96/mo now). Same payment as a year ago supports about $252,000 at 7.28%, about $28,000 less.\nBEFORE POSTING:\n• Overlap: draws on L1, FB1 and TT1 numbers; its job is the synthesis for YouTube search. Last week's YouTube covered 'reduce/relist/wait' and 'winter vs spring'; neither is repeated.\n• Freddie Mac may publish early because of Thanksgiving. If a newer PMMS is out before posting, rerun the math and update script, overlay and caption."
